## Summary

Define all WebSocket close status codes per RFC 6455 Section 7.4.1 and the IANA WebSocket Close Code Number Registry.

## Specification Reference

RFC 6455 Section 7.4.1 - Defined Status Codes:
- 1000: Normal closure
- 1001: Going away (e.g., page navigation)
- 1002: Protocol error
- 1003: Unsupported data type
- 1005: No status code (reserved, must not be sent)
- 1006: Abnormal closure (reserved, must not be sent)
- 1007: Invalid payload data (e.g., non-UTF-8 in text frame)
- 1008: Policy violation
- 1009: Message too big
- 1010: Extension required (client only)
- 1011: Internal server error
- 1015: TLS handshake failure (reserved, must not be sent)

Ranges:
- 0-999: Reserved, not used
- 1000-2999: Reserved for protocol (defined by RFC/IANA)
- 3000-3999: Reserved for libraries/frameworks
- 4000-4999: Reserved for applications (private use)

## Implementation Details

### File: src/websocket/protocol/close_codes.zig

```zig
/// WebSocket close status codes per RFC 6455 Section 7.4.1
pub const CloseCode = enum(u16) {
    /// Normal closure; the connection successfully completed
    normal_closure = 1000,

    /// Endpoint is going away (e.g., server shutdown, browser navigating)
    going_away = 1001,

    /// Protocol error encountered
    protocol_error = 1002,

    /// Received data type cannot be accepted (e.g., text-only endpoint got binary)
    unsupported_data = 1003,

    /// Reserved. Must not be sent in a close frame.
    /// Indicates no status code was present.
    no_status_received = 1005,

    /// Reserved. Must not be sent in a close frame.
    /// Indicates abnormal closure (no close frame received).
    abnormal_closure = 1006,

    /// Invalid frame payload data (e.g., non-UTF-8 in text message)
    invalid_payload_data = 1007,

    /// Generic policy violation
    policy_violation = 1008,

    /// Message is too big to process
    message_too_big = 1009,

    /// Client expected server to negotiate extension(s)
    missing_extension = 1010,

    /// Internal server error
    internal_error = 1011,

    /// Reserved. Must not be sent in a close frame.
    /// Indicates TLS handshake failure.
    tls_handshake_failure = 1015,

    /// Allow arbitrary codes in valid ranges
    _,

    /// Check if code is valid for sending in a close frame
    pub fn isValidForSending(self: CloseCode) bool {
        const code = @intFromEnum(self);
        // Cannot send reserved codes
        if (code == 1005 or code == 1006 or code == 1015) return false;
        // Valid range: 1000, or 3000-4999
        return code == 1000 or (code >= 3000 and code <= 4999);
    }

    /// Check if code is in the private use range (4000-4999)
    pub fn isPrivateUse(self: CloseCode) bool {
        const code = @intFromEnum(self);
        return code >= 4000 and code <= 4999;
    }

    /// Check if code is in the library/framework range (3000-3999)
    pub fn isLibraryRange(self: CloseCode) bool {
        const code = @intFromEnum(self);
        return code >= 3000 and code <= 3999;
    }

    /// Get human-readable description
    pub fn description(self: CloseCode) []const u8 {
        return switch (self) {
            .normal_closure => "Normal closure",
            .going_away => "Going away",
            .protocol_error => "Protocol error",
            // ... etc
            else => "Unknown close code",
        };
    }
};

/// Validate a close code from the WebSocket API
/// Per WHATWG spec: code must be 1000 or in range 3000-4999
pub fn isValidApiCloseCode(code: u16) bool {
    return code == 1000 or (code >= 3000 and code <= 4999);
}
```

