## Summary

Integrate WebSocket event dispatching with the WHATWG-compliant event loop in src/runtime/event_loop/. The spec requires all WebSocket events to be dispatched via `queue a task`.

## Specification Reference

### WHATWG WebSockets - Feedback from the protocol

> When the WebSocket connection is established, the user agent must **queue a task** to run these steps...
> When a WebSocket message has been received, the user agent must **queue a task** to follow these steps...
> When the WebSocket closing handshake is started, the user agent must **queue a task**...
> When the WebSocket connection is closed, the user agent must **queue a task**...

### WHATWG HTML - Event loops

> The **task source** for all tasks queued in this section is the **WebSocket task source**.

## Current State

- `src/runtime/event_loop/` has task queue infrastructure
- `TaskQueueSet` exists with priority-based queues
- `EventLoop.postTask()` returns `error.NotImplemented`

