Extract detailed timing information from libcurl for the Resource Timing API.

## Background
Per W3C Resource Timing spec, we need:
- DNS lookup time
- TCP connection time
- TLS handshake time
- Time to first byte
- Total transfer time

Libcurl provides all of this via CURLINFO.

## Current State
- FetchTimingInfo exists at `src/fetch/internal/fetch_timing.zig`
- ConnectionTimingInfo exists at `src/fetch/network/backend.zig`
- Only basic timing (total_time, ttfb) currently extracted

## Implementation

### Extract full timing from curl
```zig
fn extractTimingInfo(handle: *curl.CURL) ConnectionTimingInfo {
    var info: ConnectionTimingInfo = .{};

    // DNS timing
    var dns_time: f64 = 0;
    _ = curl.curl_easy_getinfo(handle, curl.CURLINFO_NAMELOOKUP_TIME, &dns_time);
    info.dns_end_ms = @intFromFloat(dns_time * 1000);

    // TCP connect timing
    var connect_time: f64 = 0;
    _ = curl.curl_easy_getinfo(handle, curl.CURLINFO_CONNECT_TIME, &connect_time);
    info.connect_end_ms = @intFromFloat(connect_time * 1000);
    info.connect_start_ms = info.dns_end_ms;

    // TLS timing (appconnect = TCP + TLS)
    var appconnect_time: f64 = 0;
    _ = curl.curl_easy_getinfo(handle, curl.CURLINFO_APPCONNECT_TIME, &appconnect_time);
    if (appconnect_time > 0) {
        info.secure_connection_start_ms = info.connect_end_ms;
    }

    // Check if connection was reused
    var reused: c_long = 0;
    _ = curl.curl_easy_getinfo(handle, curl.CURLINFO_NUM_CONNECTS, &reused);
    info.connection_reused = (reused == 0);

    return info;
}
```

### CURLINFO timing fields
| CURLINFO | Meaning |
|----------|---------|
| NAMELOOKUP_TIME | DNS resolution complete |
| CONNECT_TIME | TCP connection complete |
| APPCONNECT_TIME | TLS handshake complete |
| PRETRANSFER_TIME | Ready to transfer |
| STARTTRANSFER_TIME | First byte received |
| TOTAL_TIME | Transfer complete |
| REDIRECT_TIME | Time spent in redirects |

### Populate FetchTimingInfo
```zig
fn populateFetchTiming(
    timing_info: *FetchTimingInfo,
    connection_timing: *ConnectionTimingInfo,
    response: *NetworkResponse,
) void {
    timing_info.connection_timing = connection_timing.*;
    timing_info.final_network_request_start_time = getCurrentTimeMs() - response.total_time_ms;
    timing_info.final_network_response_start_time = 
        timing_info.final_network_request_start_time + response.time_to_first_byte_ms;
    timing_info.end_time = getCurrentTimeMs();
}
```

