Implement a pool of reusable arenas for zero-fragmentation request/transaction memory management.

**Objectives:**
- Pool of `std.heap.ArenaAllocator` instances
- Acquire/release interface
- Automatic reset on release
- Memory efficient pooling

**Files to Create:**
```
src/runtime/event_loop/mem/arena_pool.zig
tests/event_loop/arena_pool_test.zig
```

**Implementation Details:**

```zig
pub const ArenaPool = struct {
    arenas: std.ArrayList(*std.heap.ArenaAllocator),
    available: std.ArrayList(*std.heap.ArenaAllocator), // Free list
    upstream_allocator: std.mem.Allocator, // jemalloc
    mutex: std.Thread.Mutex, // Thread-safe acquire/release

    pub fn init(upstream_allocator: std.mem.Allocator, initial_capacity: usize) !ArenaPool {
        var pool = ArenaPool{
            .arenas = std.ArrayList(*std.heap.ArenaAllocator).init(upstream_allocator),
            .available = std.ArrayList(*std.heap.ArenaAllocator).init(upstream_allocator),
            .upstream_allocator = upstream_allocator,
            .mutex = .{},
        };

        // Pre-allocate initial arenas
        for (0..initial_capacity) |_| {
            const arena = try upstream_allocator.create(std.heap.ArenaAllocator);
            arena.* = std.heap.ArenaAllocator.init(upstream_allocator);
            try pool.arenas.append(arena);
            try pool.available.append(arena);
        }

        return pool;
    }

    pub fn acquire(self: *ArenaPool) !*std.heap.ArenaAllocator {
        self.mutex.lock();
        defer self.mutex.unlock();

        if (self.available.popOrNull()) |arena| {
            return arena;
        }

        // All arenas in use, allocate new one
        const arena = try self.upstream_allocator.create(std.heap.ArenaAllocator);
        arena.* = std.heap.ArenaAllocator.init(self.upstream_allocator);
        try self.arenas.append(arena);
        return arena;
    }

    pub fn release(self: *ArenaPool, arena: *std.heap.ArenaAllocator) void {
        arena.reset(.retain_capacity); // Reset without freeing backing memory

        self.mutex.lock();
        defer self.mutex.unlock();
        self.available.append(arena) catch {}; // Return to pool
    }

    pub fn deinit(self: *ArenaPool) void {
        for (self.arenas.items) |arena| {
            arena.deinit();
            self.upstream_allocator.destroy(arena);
        }
        self.arenas.deinit();
        self.available.deinit();
    }
};
```

**Testing Strategy:**
1. Acquire/release cycle
2. Grow pool when all arenas in use
3. Memory reuse (arena reset)
4. Thread safety (multiple threads acquire/release)
5. Fragmentation test (long-running)

**Acceptance Criteria:**
