### Parse Response CSP

```zig
/// Parse HTTP response headers into a CSP list.
/// Spec: CSP Level 3 § 2.2.2
///
/// Algorithm:
/// 1. Let policies be an empty list
/// 2. For each Content-Security-Policy header:
///    a. Parse with source='header', disposition='enforce'
///    b. If directive set not empty, append to policies
/// 3. For each Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only header:
///    a. Parse with source='header', disposition='report'
///    b. If directive set not empty, append to policies
/// 4. Set self-origin on all policies from response URL
/// 5. Return policies
pub fn parseResponseCSP(
    allocator: std.mem.Allocator,
    response_headers: anytype, // Header list interface
    response_url: anytype,     // URL interface
) !types.CSPList {
    var policies = types.CSPList.init(allocator);

    // Parse Content-Security-Policy headers (enforce)
    if (response_headers.getAll("Content-Security-Policy")) |csp_headers| {
        for (csp_headers) |header_value| {
            var policy = try parseSerializedCSP(
                allocator, 
                header_value, 
                .header, 
                .enforce,
            );

            if (!policy.directive_set.isEmpty()) {
                try policies.append(policy);
            } else {
                policy.deinit();
            }
        }
    }

    // Parse Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only headers (report)
    if (response_headers.getAll("Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only")) |cspro_headers| {
        for (cspro_headers) |header_value| {
            var policy = try parseSerializedCSP(
                allocator,
                header_value,
                .header,
                .report,
            );

            if (!policy.directive_set.isEmpty()) {
                try policies.append(policy);
            } else {
                policy.deinit();
            }
        }
    }

    // Set self-origin on all policies
    const self_origin = response_url.origin();
    for (policies.policies.items) |*policy| {
        policy.self_origin = self_origin;
    }

    return policies;
}
```

## Key Implementation Details

1. **Directive names are case-insensitive** - lowercase before comparison
2. **First directive wins** - duplicate directives are ignored
3. **Source expressions** - parse keywords ('self', 'unsafe-eval'), nonces, hashes, hosts, schemes
4. **Whitespace handling** - strip leading/trailing, split on whitespace
5. **Non-ASCII rejection** - skip non-ASCII tokens

