# Phase 2, Week 4: send() Algorithm - Async Path

## Overview

Implement the asynchronous send() algorithm with complete Fetch integration, response processing, and 50ms progress event throttling. This is the core of XMLHttpRequest functionality.

## Objectives

1. Implement async send() algorithm
2. Integrate with Fetch API internal infrastructure
3. Implement response processing callbacks
4. Implement progress event throttling (50ms)
5. Implement complete event sequence
6. Comprehensive tests for async requests

## Spec References

- XHR Standard (send): https://xhr.spec.whatwg.org/#the-send()-method
- XHR Standard (response): https://xhr.spec.whatwg.org/#response
- Fetch Standard: https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/

## Architecture

```
send() algorithm
    ↓
Create Fetch Request (InternalRequest)
    ↓
Start Fetch with callbacks
    ↓
Process Response (headers → HEADERS_RECEIVED)
    ↓
Process Body Chunks (accumulate → LOADING)
    ↓
Process End of Body (DONE)
    ↓
Fire Events (loadstart → progress → load → loadend)
```

