/// Parse a single range header value.
///
/// Format: bytes=START-END or bytes=START- or bytes=-END
/// Returns (rangeStart, rangeEnd) where either can be null.
///
/// Algorithm:
/// 1. If value doesn't start with "bytes", return failure
/// 2. Skip "bytes" (5 chars)
/// 3. If allowWhitespace, skip HTTP tab/space
/// 4. If char != '=', return failure
/// 5. Advance, skip whitespace if allowed
/// 6. Collect digits for rangeStart
/// 7. Skip whitespace if allowed
/// 8. If char != '-', return failure
/// 9. Advance, skip whitespace if allowed
/// 10. Collect digits for rangeEnd
/// 11. If not at end, return failure
/// 12. If both null, return failure
/// 13. If both set and start > end, return failure
/// 14. Return (rangeStart, rangeEnd)
